# Template drift allowlist for zmanuals-doc.
# Generated projects start from create-zudo-doc templates; this file lists
# intentional divergences from the pinned create-zudo-doc baseline so
# `check-template-drift.sh` (pnpm check:template-drift) exits 0.
#
# Format: one repo-relative path per line (no leading slash).
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
# Paths are relative to doc/ (the workspace package root).
#
# STATUS (1.2.0 clean-room migration):
#   All 82 drifted files fall into two categories:
#
#   A. Prettier reformatting only — The scaffold applies the project's
#      Prettier config (single-quotes, different line-wrap thresholds) over
#      the template source which ships with double-quotes. No intentional
#      code changes; these files ARE the template content, just differently
#      formatted. If create-zudo-doc adopts single-quote style in a future
#      release, these entries can be deleted.
#
#   B. Intentional project additions — Files where actual content was added
#      beyond what the template ships (e.g. global.css has the doc-history
#      diff-viewer styles that were generated into the @slot:feature-styles
#      placeholder, tsconfig.json has a project-specific exclude list).
#
#   C. Build artifact — .zfb/doc-history-meta.json is written at build time;
#      the template ships {} but production has real metadata.
#
# No files here are intentional component FORKS (that would require ejection
# and an entry in .zudo-doc.json). All differences are either formatting,
# project-specific content additions, or build artifacts.

# ── B. Intentional project additions (content beyond the template) ─────────
# run-b4push.sh: extended with step 4 (link check via check-links.js)
# on top of the scaffold's 4-step baseline (check, build, html-validate, smoke).
